title: Implement PackageId-based symbol mangling in codegen
status: complete
atomic: true
priority: medium
blocked_by: []
created_at: '2026-06-15T05:51:53'
updated_at: '2026-06-17T06:31:50'
result: 'Codegen now mangles symbols by owning package per scope.md §1.3: Compiler::mangle_symbol
  prepends <pkgid_hash>_ (8 hex of semantic_hash) to the existing <module>_<name>,
  applied at both non-main add_function sites in declare_mir_fn. Mangling is gated
  on a new is_multi_package flag (= !prog.module_pkgs.is_empty()); the single-package
  fast path emits bare names unchanged (verified via --emit-llvm: @helper/@main bare),
  so 98% of programs see zero change. main (C entry) and lib_mode (FFI surface) are
  never mangled. Call resolution is unaffected because it keys self.fns by Symbol,
  not the LLVM symbol name. 6 mangling unit tests cover format (8-hex prefix), distinctness
  across coexisting versions, promotion (equal-identity → one symbol), and the main/lib/single-package
  exemptions. Surfaced and documented that multi-version distinctness derives from
  the (name,scope,version) intern key, not source-hash. 315 lib tests + access_semantics
  + concurrency_shutdown green; no new regressions.'
description: Replace flat module_name mangling with <pkgid-hash>_<module>_<name> scheme
  in codegen. Done when emitted symbols use the new mangling, multi-version symbols
  are distinct, and mangling tests verify the format and uniqueness. Depends on MIR
  threading and semantic_hash subtasks.
